{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg --files -g AGENTS.md test src | head -50 && git log -3 --oneline && cat deps.edn'","aggregated_output":"7ab37566 docs(collab): reply to the yang.clojure seat — the per-frontend equality-gate scope adopted for the php/ts adoption rounds\n7c09c819 docs(exception-track): the peer relays — to yang.clojure (R3 then R4), to ts/php (JS first, PHP the coherent round), to jolt (awareness; the kit-growth heads-up)\n4879edef docs(exception-track): the ruling v2 — all three review verdicts folded (R3 all four frontends, lifetime explicit, corrected sequencing, widened gate, citation corrections); v1 superseded\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \"0.1.30\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\n        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\n        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \"1.3\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\n ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"\n         \"build/antlr/python3/classes\" \"build/antlr/php/classes\"\n         \"build/antlr/typescript/classes\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}\n                               ;; latte-kernel: the LaTTe proof assistant's kernel,\n                               ;; the differential oracle for the yang.clojure gap\n                               ;; program (pinned; MIT; dependency-free)\n                               latte-kernel/latte-kernel\n                               {:git/url \"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\"\n                                :git/sha \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"}}\n                  ;; The guest recursion limit allows depth that needs more than the\n                  ;; JVM's platform default thread stack (1024 KB on Linux, 2048 KB on\n                  ;; macOS): under 1 MB the guard loses to a JVM StackOverflowError\n                  ;; before it can raise Python's RecursionError, so the same tests\n                  ;; pass on macOS and fail on Linux. 4 MB is twice the measured\n                  ;; macOS-default minimum, leaving headroom as the prelude grows.\n                  ;; Evidence: docs/agents/known-gaps.md (the recursion rows).\n                  ;; merged stack policy: -Xss64m supersedes the earlier -Xss4m —\n                  ;; deep assertion payloads (the PHPT selection diagnostics and\n                  ;; the conformance compositions) overflow smaller stacks in\n                  ;; clojure.test's printer on shiva (verified green at -Xss64m;\n                  ;; the 4m minimum for the prelude recursion rows still holds)\n                  :jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\" \"build/antlr/python3/js\"]\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\n           :dev {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}\n                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\n                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\n                              ;; generator only; production uses\n                              ;; dao.data.btree\n                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                              {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                 :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]}\n           ;; The one ClojureDart pin. Compose it with the build aliases:\n           ;; clj -M:clojuredart:cljd ..., clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build ...\n           :clojuredart {:extra-deps {sonwh98/clojuredart\n                                      {:git/url \"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\"\n                                       :sha \"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\"}\n                                      }}\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}}\n                    :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]\n                    :main-opts [\"-m\" \"world.server\"]}\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"]}\n           ;; jolt host configuration (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\n           ;; §4.2-4.3), run through build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt.\n           ;; src/jolt precedes src/cljc so a host override wins; src/clj is\n           ;; listed for audited portable namespaces only (its JVM namespaces\n           ;; are selected away by :jolt reader branches, never loaded). No\n           ;; generated Java parser classes, no JS/Dart roots, and no\n           ;; dependency coordinate is fetched until a jolt-loaded namespace\n           ;; needs one.\n           :jolt {:replace-paths [\"src/jolt\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/clj\"]\n                  :replace-deps {}}\n           :jolt-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"]}\n           ;; composed after :jolt (-M:jolt:jolt-test): the oracle tests and\n           ;; src/dev (src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj and its sentinel)\n           :jolt-test {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]}\n           ;; DIAGNOSTIC only (-M:jolt:jolt-diag:jolt-test): a jolt stand-in\n           ;; for the corpus loader dao.jing.cbor-fixtures, whose root must\n           ;; precede test (src/dev/jolt_diag/dao/jing/cbor_fixtures.cljc);\n           ;; jolt puts :extra-paths roots first, in alias order (-Spath)\n           :jolt-diag {:extra-paths [\"src/dev/jolt_diag\"]}\n           :cljs-yin-repl\n           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.node-runner\"]}\n           :fmt {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :exec-fn tasks/fix-all}\n           ;; Build-time generation of the grammars-v4 Python3 parser.\n           ;; The tool version must equal the antlr4-runtime above.\n           :antlr-gen {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                       :extra-deps {org.antlr/antlr4 {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}}\n                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yang-antlr-gen\"]}\n           :kondo {:extra-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version \"2026.01.19\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"clj-kondo.main\"]}\n           ;; Development/oracle only (datomic-q-v1 Client oracle runner,\n           ;; docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md); never a production\n           ;; dependency. Backend deps/config are pinned separately once selected.\n           :oracle {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\" \"test\"]\n                    :extra-deps {com.datomic/client-api {:mvn/version \"1.0.69\"}\n                                 ;; oracle backend: Datomic Local, in-process,\n                                 ;; run in docker/oracle (dev-scope only)\n                                 com.datomic/local {:mvn/version \"1.0.301\"}}}\n           :dbg {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                 :main-opts [\"-m\" \"debug-cljd\"]\n                 :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :cljd-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.runner\"]}\n           :cljd-yin-repl-build\n           {:main-opts  [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n            :cljd/opts  {:kind       :dart\n                         :main       yin.repl.main\n                         :output-dir \"build/yin-repl\"\n                         :output-to  \"build/yin-repl/yin_repl.dart\"}}\n           :dep-graph {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                       :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}}\n                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"dep-graph\"]}}}\n\n\n;; clj -X:fmt\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL:server\n;; clj -M:test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-literal-test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-continuation-test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.repl.python-antlr-test\n;; clj -X:test :nses '[yin.vm-literal-test yin.vm-test]'\n;; clj -M:test -v yin.vm-addition-test/test-lambda-with-multiple-operations\n\n;; clj -X:clean\n\n;; npx shadow-cljs compile test && node target/node-tests.js\n;; npx shadow-cljs release demo\n;; clj -M:dev -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release demo\n\n\n;; mise exec -- clj -M:clojuredart:cljd watch \n;; mise exec -- flutter run \n\n;; To start the emulator:                                                                                              ;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34\n;; flutter emulators --launch Pixel_3_API_34\n;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34 -no-snapshot-load  \n;; emulator -list-avds\n\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph                    # full report + dep-graph.dot + dep-graph.svg\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph --filter \"yin.*\"   # only yin namespaces\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph --layout circo     # choose graphviz layout engine\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3838,3912p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; sed -n '4016,4090p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; cat test/yang/python/antlr/call_entry_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3838,3912p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; sed -n '4016,4090p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; cat test/yang/python/antlr/call_entry_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"#### 8.10.7 Normal return and escaping conditions\n\nNormal return is the value of ordinary Yin application. There is no\nextra return continuation, completion packet around each result, or new\nlanguage-specific return instruction.\n\nAn escaping source exception invokes the supplied raise exit with:\n\n```clojure\n{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n :yang.call/value  original-thrown-value}\n```\n\nThis is the argument to an exceptional continuation transfer, not an\nordinary return. Returning an identical-looking map returns normal data.\nLikewise, a source program throwing a map with these keys throws that\nmap as the **payload of a new condition**; its shape is never evidence\nthat it is already a condition to forward. No engine-effect value is\nsynthesized.\n\nProtocol failures use qualified reasons such as\n`:yang.call/not-callable`, `:yang.call/invalid-invocation`, and\n`:yang.call/unsupported-binding`, with plain evidence. The caller maps\nthem to a documented local exception form retaining the complete\noriginal condition. Callee argument-binding failures retain the actual\ncallee exception under `:yang.call/thrown`. These reasons do not extend\n`dao.stream`'s outcome algebra.\n\nThe receiving caller interprets an escaping exception as follows:\n\n1. A payload valid as an exception in its own runtime retains that\n   runtime's ordinary catching and identity behavior.\n2. A runtime permitting arbitrary thrown values, such as JavaScript,\n   may deliver the original payload directly.\n3. A runtime requiring exception objects, such as Python or PHP,\n   represents an otherwise foreign payload with its own\n   `ForeignException`, retaining the complete condition and original\n   payload. Catch-all catches this local object. Typed source catches\n   match its local hierarchy, never guessed foreign class names.\n\n`ForeignException` is a proposed prelude-owned type, not a VM type.\nUnchanged rethrow propagates the original condition without adding\nwrappers. Raising a new exception creates a new condition. Crossing back\ninto a runtime recognizing the original exception restores its original\ntype and identity. Formatting a foreign payload must not implicitly\ninvoke a foreign method.\n\nThe runtime associates its generated wrapper's identity with the retained\ncondition for the wrapper's entire lifetime, separate from source-writable\nattributes. The association normally lives in private wrapper-cell\ncontents, or an equivalent task-owned identity structure with the same\nlifetime. It survives storing or returning the wrapper after the creating\ncall/catch activation has ended, and remains recoverable when that same\nwrapper is rethrown in another activation. Temporary catch state alone is\ninsufficient. Reachability/reclamation must retain the condition and its\npayload while the wrapper is live, without an ambient registry.\n\nThe runtime must not detect wrappers or unwrap arbitrary maps by their\nkey names. JavaScript may expose raw payloads for\n`:yang.call/thrown`; its local exception for a protocol failure must still\nretain that failure's qualified condition. Rethrowing the same generated\nexception forwards that complete condition, including protocol reasons;\nthrowing an unrelated value creates a new `:yang.call/thrown` condition.\nSaved activation state refers to this identity-owned association; exiting\nor restoring a catch does not destroy it.\n\nVM application/custody defects and host implementation failures remain\noperational failures. Do not catch them broadly and relabel them as\nsource exceptions. Existing explicit stream/module refusals keep their\nsource mappings under the relevant profiles.\n\n#### 8.10.8 Cleanup, re-entry, and suspension\n\nEach activation establishes its own exception bridge and saves its\ncallee runtime's dynamic context. Binding, body, and exit run under that\n#### 8.10.11 Acceptance gates\n\nExecute real lowered source bodies, not only synthetic functions with\nthe expected slot. A harness may compose published exports and namespace\nprojections explicitly. It must not rewrite call nodes, extract foreign\n`:code`, or insert test-local language-pair wrappers to make calls work.\n\nRequired evidence:\n\n- **Local semantics:** existing suites preserve argument order, defaults,\n  required/extra arguments, keyword errors, receivers, exceptions, and\n  supported reference/static behavior.\n- **Direct calls:** each implemented frontend calls every other\n  conforming frontend through the same mechanism in both directions\n  with compatible values. Derive the test matrix from admitted\n  frontends; do not hard-code it into runtime dispatch.\n- **Higher-order calls:** pass, return, store, recurse, and call back\n  through received functions. Assert identity and captures without\n  replacement cells.\n- **Callable admission:** source data with an entry-spelled property\n  remains data; profile-constructed descriptors are admitted. Exercise\n  supported PHP string/array designators both under local resolution and\n  explicit callable export, preserving required late lookup without\n  foreign namespace guessing.\n- **Presence and binding:** distinguish missing from explicit\n  null/None/undefined; retain duplicate keywords until binding; supply\n  bound self once; evaluate receiver/spreads/defaults at source-defined\n  times and counts.\n- **Dynamic callability:** where supported, an existing instance becomes\n  eligible after its class gains a call method and ineligible after\n  deletion. Calls whose arguments change this metadata observe the\n  correct source-required lookup time without instance rewrapping.\n- **Opaque values:** round-trip foreign objects, functions, strings,\n  float64 content, and exact integers unchanged. Assert aliasing and no\n  silent rounding/null conversion. Unsupported operations yield\n  documented guest errors.\n- **References:** absent/incompatible writable-location profiles fail\n  before reference acquisition and the body, with no reference-induced\n  writeback. Source-required side effects from evaluating arguments still\n  occur; rejection must not erase them. Compatible profiles prove\n  mutation, aliasing, cleanup, and suspension behavior.\n- **Exceptions:** cover binding failures, arbitrary foreign thrown data,\n  catch-all/typed catches, unchanged rethrow, replacement in `finally`,\n  protocol-error rethrow, condition-shaped thrown maps, and A-to-B-to-A\n  propagation. Assert original exception identity and cleanup order,\n  not only rendered text. Store/return a generated `ForeignException`,\n  finish its creating activation, then rethrow it from another activation\n  and assert recovery of the original condition and payload identity.\n- **Context lifetime:** repeated success/raise/success, cross-runtime\n  recursion, and stream suspension/resume restore handler/depth/frame\n  state and perform arguments/cleanup exactly once. Entry boilerplate\n  must not double-count source recursion or tracing activations.\n- **Publication/custody:** bundled/linked forms agree; two importing\n  tasks have independent state. Existing gates still refuse foreign-task\n  cells, forged refs, host functions, and inadmissible continuations.\n- **Portability:** execute portable packet-to-UAST fixtures on JVM,\n  Node, and Dart over the four VMs wherever existing contracts admit\n  the program. JVM-only parsers may supply checked-in CST fixtures;\n  parser availability is distinct from calling conformance.\n\nReport callable kinds, binding/value extensions, actual host/VM\ncoverage as an explicit host-by-VM matrix, refusals, and remaining gaps\nper frontend revision. A scalar example or common UAST grammar alone\ndoes not establish conformance.\n\n#### 8.10.12 Cell-reference call routing and authenticity\n\nRuling of record (2026-11-04, owner-approved). A cross-language\nreference is a cell-ref map the VM issues (`{:type :cell-ref :id\n:cell-N :seal s}`). In Clojure a map is callable, so the call lowering\nmust route a callee between reference semantics and data semantics.\nThree rounds routed by value shape at call time (key presence,\nexact shape, minted-id language) and each left the same defect class:\ninnocent data whose shape imitates the reference language aborted at\n`cell/get` instead of answering as data. The defect is structural — a\n(ns yang.python.antlr.call-entry-test\n  \"Python function binder fixtures and source-call helper coverage for the\n   shared call runtime. The binder fixtures prove the record/constructor\n   contract only; they are not conformance evidence under docs/design/yang.antlr.md §8.10.11.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n            [yang.python.antlr.int-ops-test :as ops]\n            [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as prelude]))\n\n\n(def ^:private bindings\n  '[raise-exit (fn [condition] condition)\n    record (fn [f positional named]\n             (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/callee f)\n                                  :yang.call/positional positional)\n                           :yang.call/named named)\n                    :yang.call/raise raise-exit))\n    invoke (fn [f positional named]\n             ((get (cell/get f) :yang.call/entry) (record f positional named)))\n    positional (py/make-function \"positional\" {:params [\"x\"]} [] []\n                                 (fn [args] (get args 0)))\n    named (py/make-function \"named\" {:params [\"x\" \"y\"]} [] []\n                            (fn [args] (get args 1)))\n    defaulted (py/make-function \"defaulted\" {:params [\"x\"]} [7] []\n                                (fn [args] (get args 0)))\n    variadic (py/make-function \"variadic\" {:params [\"x\"] :star? true} [] []\n                               (fn [args] (get (get args 1) :items)))\n    duplicate (py/make-function \"duplicate\" {:params [\"x\"]} [] []\n                                (fn [args] (get args 0)))\n    substituted (py/make-function \"substituted\" {:params [\"x\"]} [] []\n                                  (fn [args] (get args 0)))\n    receiver-fn (py/make-function \"receiver\" {:params [\"x\"]} [] []\n                                  (fn [args] (get args 0)))\n    profile-fn (py/make-function \"profile\" {:params [\"x\"]} [] []\n                                 (fn [args] (get args 0)))\n    caught (fn [thunk]\n             (py/try thunk\n                     (fn [e] (get (cell/get (get (cell/get e) :class)) :name))\n                     (fn [] :py/None)))])\n\n\n(def ^:private result-expressions\n  '[(if (get (cell/get positional) :yang.call/entry) true false)\n    (if (get (cell/get py.b/len) :yang.call/entry) true false)\n    (if (get (cell/get py.b/TypeError) :yang.call/entry) true false)\n    (let [absent (record positional [] [])\n          supplied (assoc (record positional [] []) :yang.call/receiver :py/None)]\n      (py/vconj (py/vconj [] (get absent :yang.call/receiver :py/missing))\n                (get supplied :yang.call/receiver :py/missing)))\n    (invoke positional [4] [])\n    (invoke named [1] [[\"y\" 9]])\n    (invoke defaulted [] [])\n    (invoke defaulted [:py/None] [])\n    (invoke variadic [1 2 3] [])\n    (let [r (invoke duplicate [1] [[\"x\" 2]])\n          e (get r :yang.call/value)]\n      (py/vconj (py/vconj [] (get r :yang.call/reason))\n                (get (cell/get (get (cell/get e) :class)) :name)))\n    (get ((get (cell/get positional) :yang.call/entry)\n          (record substituted [5] []))\n         :yang.call/reason)\n    (invoke receiver-fn [11] [])\n    ((get (cell/get receiver-fn) :yang.call/entry)\n     (assoc (record receiver-fn [12] []) :yang.call/receiver :py/None))\n    (get ((get (cell/get profile-fn) :yang.call/entry)\n          (assoc (record profile-fn [3] []) :yang.call/binding-profile :py/None))\n         :yang.call/reason)])\n\n\n(def ^:private fixtures\n  (list 'let bindings\n        (reduce (fn [acc expression] (list 'py/vconj acc expression))\n                []\n                result-expressions)))\n\n\n(deftest python-function-entry-record-contract-test\n  (let [expected [true false false [:py/missing :py/None]\n                  4 9 7 :py/None [2 3]\n                  [:yang.call/thrown \"TypeError\"]\n                  :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                  11 12 :yang.call/unsupported-binding]]\n    (doseq [[backend result] (ops/run-with-prelude prelude/uast fixtures)]\n      (is (= expected result) (str backend)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private fixture\n  '(let [python-fn (py/make-function \"python\" {:params [\"x\" \"y\"]} [7] []\n                                     (fn [args] (get args 1)))\n         foreign-fn (assoc {}\n                           :yang.call/entry\n                           (fn [invocation]\n                             (get (get invocation :yang.call/positional) 0)))\n         call-python (py/call-kw python-fn [1] [])\n         call-named (py/call-kw python-fn [1] [[\"y\" 9]])\n         call-foreign (py/call foreign-fn [42])\n         not-callable (py/try (fn [] (py/call-kw {} [] []))\n                              (fn [e] (get (cell/get (get (cell/get e) :class)) :name))\n                              (fn [] :py/None))]\n     (py/vconj (py/vconj (py/vconj [] call-python) call-named)\n               (py/vconj (py/vconj [] call-foreign) not-callable))))\n\n\n(deftest python-source-calls-use-shared-entry-test\n  (doseq [[backend result] (ops/run-with-prelude prelude/uast fixture)]\n    (is (= [7 9 [42 \"TypeError\"]] result) (str backend))))\n\n\n(deftest python-cross-frontend-callable-identity-test\n  (let [fixture\n        '(let [php-function\n               (cell/new\n                 (assoc {:php/type :function}\n                        :yang.call/entry\n                        (fn [invocation]\n                          (get invocation :yang.call/callee))))\n               returned (py/call-kw php-function [] [])]\n           (if (= php-function returned) :same :different))]\n    (doseq [[backend result] (ops/run-with-prelude prelude/uast fixture)]\n      (is (= :same result) (str backend)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' test/yang/core/call_test.cljc; cat src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/render.cljc; rg -n 'defn (output|render)|snapshot' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/render.cljc test/yang/php/antlr/portable_harness.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' test/yang/core/call_test.cljc; cat src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/render.cljc; rg -n 'defn (output|render)|snapshot' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/render.cljc test/yang/php/antlr/portable_harness.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.core.call-test\n  \"Synthetic guest proof for the language-neutral calling runtime.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n            [yang.core.uast :as u]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(def ^:private registry\n  (-> (module/empty-registry)\n      module/register-cell-module\n      data/register-data-module))\n\n\n(def ^:private opts\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n   :capability-secret tu/secret\n   :primitives vm/primitives\n   :modules registry})\n\n\n(def ^:private load-semantic-ast\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast vm/ast-contract))\n\n\n(def ^:private runners\n  {:ast-walker (fn [ast] (vm/eval (tu/create-vm opts) ast))\n   :semantic (fn [ast]\n               (vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                                          (vm/ast->datoms ast))))\n   :stack (fn [ast]\n            (vm/run (dvm/create-vm\n                      (:image (derive/stack-image\n                                (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n                      (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract))))\n   :register (fn [ast]\n               (vm/run (rvm/create-vm\n                         (derive/register-image\n                           (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\n                         (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract))))})\n\n\n(defn- run-everywhere\n  [emitter form]\n  (let [ast (u/mark-tails (u/then emitter (u/sexp->uast form)))]\n    (into {}\n          (map (fn [[engine run]] [engine (vm/value (run ast))]))\n          runners)))\n\n\n(deftest base-validation-and-construction-test\n  (testing \"required fields, ordered names, duplicate names and receiver presence\"\n    (is (every? true?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(yang.call/valid-invocation?\n                           {:yang.call/callee :f\n                            :yang.call/positional []\n                            :yang.call/named [[\"x\" 1] [\"x\" 2]]\n                            :yang.call/raise :exit\n                            :yang.call/receiver nil})))))\n    (is (every? false?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(yang.call/valid-invocation?\n                           {:yang.call/callee :f\n                            :yang.call/positional []\n                            :yang.call/named [[1 :bad]]\n                            :yang.call/raise :exit})))))\n    (is (every? false?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(yang.call/valid-invocation?\n                           {:yang.call/callee :f\n                            :yang.call/positional nil\n                            :yang.call/named []\n                            :yang.call/raise :exit}))))))\n  (testing \"invocation-with retains optional fields and cannot replace core fields\"\n    (is (every? true?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(let [record\n                               (yang.call/invocation-with\n                                 :callee [] [] :exit\n                                 {:yang.call/receiver nil\n                                  :yang.call/callee :substitute})]\n                           (if (= :callee (get record :yang.call/callee))\n                             (if (data/contains? record :yang.call/receiver)\n                               (nil? (get record :yang.call/receiver))\n                               false)\n                             false))))))))\n\n\n(deftest entry-and-invocation-test\n  (testing \"descriptor entry, eligibility, original identity and unchanged result\"\n    (is (every? true?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(let [callee {:opaque [1 2]}\n                               descriptor\n                               (assoc {}\n                                      :yang.call/entry\n                                      (fn [inv]\n                                        (get inv :yang.call/callee)))]\n                           (yang.call/eligible? descriptor))))))\n    (let [payload [1 2]]\n      (is (every? #(= payload %)\n                  (vals (run-everywhere\n                          call/uast\n                          '(let [callee (assoc {} :opaque [1 2])\n                                 descriptor\n                                 (assoc callee\n                                        :yang.call/entry\n                                        (fn [inv]\n                                          (get (get inv :yang.call/callee)\n                                               :opaque)))]\n                             (yang.call/invoke descriptor [] []\n                                               (fn [condition]\n                                                 condition)))))))))\n  (testing \"cell-backed entry lookup and an ineligible descriptor\"\n    (is (every? true?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(let [descriptor\n                               (cell/new\n                                 (assoc {}\n                                        :yang.call/entry\n                                        (fn [inv] :called)))\n                               ineligible\n                               (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/entry\n                                             (fn [inv] :wrong))\n                                      :yang.call/eligible?\n                                      (fn [callee] false))\n                               called\n                               (yang.call/invoke\n                                 descriptor [] []\n                                 (fn [condition] condition))\n                               result\n                               (yang.call/invoke\n                                 ineligible [] []\n                                 (fn [condition] condition))]\n                           (if (= :called called)\n                             (= :yang.call/not-callable\n                                (get result :yang.call/reason))\n                             false))))))))\n\n\n(deftest conditions-and-transfer-test\n  (testing \"throwing wraps condition-shaped data; normal return remains data\"\n    (is (every? true?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(let [payload {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n                                        :yang.call/value :inner}\n                               result (yang.call/thrown payload)]\n                           (if (= payload (get result :yang.call/value))\n                             (= :yang.call/thrown\n                                (get result :yang.call/reason))\n                             false)))))))\n  (testing \"transfer applies the supplied exit once\"\n    (is (every? #(= {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable\n                     :yang.call/data {:callee :value}\n                     :seen true}\n                    %)\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(yang.call/transfer\n                           (fn [condition]\n                             (assoc condition :seen true))\n                           (yang.call/condition :yang.call/not-callable\n                                                {:callee :value})))))))\n  (testing \"bundled and linked emitters use the same definition source\"\n    (is (= call/module-uast\n           (core/module-tree\n             (core/module-definitions \"yang.call\" :yang.call/uninit\n                                      [] call/definitions)\n             [])))\n    (is (= call/module-exports\n           (:exports (call/module-spec registry))))\n    (is (= call/host-names\n           (set (filter namespace\n                        (keys (:primitives (call/module-spec registry)))))))\n    (is (every? true?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/module-uast\n                        '(valid-invocation?\n                           {:yang.call/callee :f\n                            :yang.call/positional []\n                            :yang.call/named []\n                            :yang.call/raise :exit})))))))\n\n\n(deftest cross-frontend-callable-identity-fixture-test\n  (testing \"a stored PHP function crosses a TS entry, is called, and stays same-cell\"\n    (let [results (run-everywhere\n                    call/uast\n                    '(let [php-function\n                           (cell/new\n                             (assoc {:php/type :function}\n                                    :yang.call/entry\n                                    (fn [invocation]\n                                      (get invocation :yang.call/callee))))\n                           stored (cell/new php-function)\n                           original (cell/get stored)\n                           typescript-relay\n                           (assoc {}\n                                  :yang.call/entry\n                                  (fn [invocation]\n                                    (yang.call/invoke\n                                      (get invocation :yang.call/receiver)\n                                      [] []\n                                      (get invocation :yang.call/raise))))\n                           returned\n                           (yang.call/invoke-with\n                             typescript-relay [] []\n                             (fn [condition] condition)\n                             (assoc {} :yang.call/receiver original))]\n                       (if (= original returned) :same :different)))]\n      (is (every? #{:same} (vals results))\n          (pr-str results))))\n  (testing \"Python calls a TS entry, receives a callback, then calls the PHP entry\"\n    (let [results\n          (run-everywhere\n            call/uast\n            '(let [php-function\n                   (cell/new\n                     (assoc {:php/type :function}\n                            :yang.call/entry\n                            (fn [invocation]\n                              (get invocation :yang.call/callee))))\n                   python-function (cell/new {:py/type :function})\n(ns yang.python.antlr.render\n  \"Python text for the values a program printed, derived at the boundary\n   from the plain-data snapshots `py/print` collects (the same place owner\n   decision 2 puts traceback line numbers). Portable and deterministic: a\n   float arrives tagged `{:py/float x}`, so `4/2` prints `2.0` on every\n   host, JS included.\n\n   Float repr is CPython's on every host and for every double: the\n   shortest round-trip digits come from the `integer` module's\n   `float-digits` (version 4), never from host `str`, in fixed notation\n   when the decimal exponent is from -4 to 15 and in exponent notation\n   otherwise.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [yin.vm.data :as data]\n    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]))\n\n\n(def ^:private exact\n  \"The `integer` exports with limits no snapshot reaches: the renderer\n   writes an integer's exact decimal with no digit limit, as CPython\n   3.9.6 prints it (a limit on `print` belongs to guest `str`), and a\n   float's shortest digits.\"\n  (integer/integer-module {::integer/max-bits 9007199254740991,\n                           ::integer/max-digits 9007199254740991}))\n\n\n(defn- negative-zero?\n  [x]\n  (and (zero? x) (neg? (/ 1.0 x))))\n\n\n(defn- zeros\n  [n]\n  (apply str (repeat n \"0\")))\n\n\n(defn- exponent-text\n  \"CPython's exponent: `e`, a sign, and at least two digits.\"\n  [e]\n  (let [digits (str (if (neg? e) (- e) e))]\n    (str (if (neg? e) \"e-\" \"e+\")\n         (if (< (count digits) 2) (str \"0\" digits) digits))))\n\n\n(defn- digits-repr\n  \"CPython's `repr` of |v| = d1.d2...dn x 10^`e`: fixed notation when\n   -4 <= e < 16, with `.0` when there is no fraction, else `d[.ddd]`\n   and the exponent.\"\n  [digits e]\n  (let [n (count digits)]\n    (cond\n      (and (<= 0 e) (< e 16))\n      (if (<= n (inc e))\n        (str digits (zeros (- (inc e) n)) \".0\")\n        (str (subs digits 0 (inc e)) \".\" (subs digits (inc e))))\n      (and (<= -4 e) (< e 0))\n      (str \"0.\" (zeros (dec (- e))) digits)\n      :else\n      (str (subs digits 0 1)\n           (when (> n 1) (str \".\" (subs digits 1)))\n           (exponent-text e)))))\n\n\n(defn float-repr\n  \"Python repr of float `f`, a host number or float64 content (on JS,\n   Jing's carrier).\"\n  [f]\n  (let [x (data/float-value f)]\n    (cond\n      #?(:cljd (.-isNaN ^num x)\n         :clj (Double/isNaN x)\n         :cljs (js/isNaN x))\n      \"nan\"\n      (= x ##Inf) \"inf\"\n      (= x ##-Inf) \"-inf\"\n      (zero? x) (if (negative-zero? x) \"-0.0\" \"0.0\")\n      :else (let [[digits e] ((get exact 'float-digits) x)]\n              (str (when (neg? x) \"-\") (digits-repr digits e))))))\n\n\n(declare repr)\n\n\n(defn- code-unit\n  [s i]\n  #?(:cljd (.codeUnitAt ^String s i)\n     :clj (int (.charAt ^String s (int i)))\n     :cljs (.charCodeAt s i)))\n\n\n(defn- hex2\n  [n]\n  (let [digits \"0123456789abcdef\"]\n    (str (subs digits (quot n 16) (inc (quot n 16)))\n         (subs digits (rem n 16) (inc (rem n 16))))))\n\n\n(defn string-repr\n  \"Python's str repr: single quotes unless the text has a single quote and\n   no double quote; backslash, the quote, \\\\n \\\\r \\\\t and other control\n   characters escaped.\"\n  [s]\n  (let [q (if (and (str/includes? s \"'\") (not (str/includes? s \"\\\"\"))) \"\\\"\" \"'\")]\n    (str q\n         (apply str\n                (map (fn [i]\n                       (let [c (code-unit s i)\n                             ch (subs s i (inc i))]\n                         (cond\n                           (= ch \"\\\\\") \"\\\\\\\\\"\n                           (= ch q) (str \"\\\\\" q)\n                           (= c 10) \"\\\\n\"\n                           (= c 13) \"\\\\r\"\n                           (= c 9) \"\\\\t\"\n                           (or (< c 32) (= c 127)) (str \"\\\\x\" (hex2 c))\n                           :else ch)))\n                     (range (count s))))\n         q)))\n\n\n(defn- seq-repr\n  [open close xs]\n  (str open (str/join \", \" (map repr xs)) close))\n\n\n(defn repr\n  \"Python `repr` of one snapshot value.\"\n  [v]\n  (cond\n    (nil? v) \"None\"\n    (true? v) \"True\"\n    (false? v) \"False\"\n    (string? v) (string-repr v)\n    ;; every exact carrier, a JS or Dart BigInt included, which `number?`\n    ;; misses\n    ((get exact 'integer?) v) ((get exact 'format) v)\n    (number? v) (str v)\n    (vector? v) (seq-repr \"[\" \"]\" v)\n    (map? v)\n    (cond\n      (contains? v :py/float) (float-repr (:py/float v))\n      (contains? v :py/tuple) (let [xs (:py/tuple v)]\n                                (if (= 1 (count xs))\n                                  (str \"(\" (repr (first xs)) \",)\")\n                                  (seq-repr \"(\" \")\" xs)))\n      (contains? v :py/dict) (str \"{\"\n                                  (str/join \", \"\n                                            (map (fn [[k x]]\n                                                   (str (repr k) \": \" (repr x)))\n                                                 (:py/dict v)))\n                                  \"}\")\n      (contains? v :py/range) (let [[a b s] (:py/range v)]\n                                (if (= 1 s)\n                                  (str \"range(\" a \", \" b \")\")\n                                  (str \"range(\" a \", \" b \", \" s \")\")))\n      (contains? v :py/set) (if (empty? (:py/set v))\n                              \"set()\"\n                              (seq-repr \"{\" \"}\" (:py/set v)))\n      (contains? v :py/instance) (str \"<\" (:py/instance v) \" object>\")\n      ;; CPython prints an address; a snapshot has none, so the text is\n      ;; the deterministic form without it\n      (contains? v :py/generator) (str \"<generator object \" (:py/generator v) \">\")\n      (contains? v :py/iterator) (str \"<\" (:py/iterator v) \" object>\")\n      (contains? v :py/class) (str \"<class '\" (:py/class v) \"'>\")\n      ;; C4 I1: the uniform module repr; CPython's built-in marker is not\n      ;; distinguished\n      (contains? v :py/module) (str \"<module '\" (:py/module v) \"'>\")\n      (contains? v :py/function) (str \"<function \" (:py/function v) \">\")\n      :else (pr-str v))\n    (= :py/method v) \"<bound method>\"\n    :else (pr-str v)))\n\n\n(defn py-str\n  \"Python `str` of one snapshot value: a string prints bare.\"\n  [v]\n  (if (string? v) v (repr v)))\n\n\n(defn line\n  \"One `print` call's text: its arguments' `str`, space separated.\"\n  [values]\n  (str/join \" \" (map py-str values)))\n\n\n(defn output\n  \"A program value's printed lines as text, exception kept as data.\"\n  [{:py/keys [out exception]}]\n  {:py/out (mapv line out), :py/exception exception})\ntest/yang/php/antlr/portable_harness.cljc:114:(defn render\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/render.cljc:3:   from the plain-data snapshots `js/log!` collects (docs/design/\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/render.cljc:21:  \"The `integer` exports with limits no snapshot reaches: the renderer\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/render.cljc:114:  \"util.inspect of one snapshot value as `console.log` shows it as a\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/render.cljc:134:  \"ToString of one snapshot value, as the uncaught line prints a thrown\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/render.cljc:157:(defn output\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:3023:(defn output\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
