{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_284","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re,collections\nroot=Path('test/yang/call')\nfull=Path('/tmp/exception-r0-runtime.log').read_text()\nrerun=Path('/tmp/exception-r0-ts-python.log').read_text()\n\ndef rows(s,prefix):\n return [line[len(prefix):] for line in s.splitlines() if line.startswith(prefix)]\ndef row_id(row):\n return re.search(r':id\\\\s+(:[\"'^'\"\\\\s,]+|\\\\[[\"'^'\"\\\\]]+\\\\])',row).group(1)\ndef status(row):\n part=row[row.rindex(':status'):]\n states=re.findall(r':(?:register|semantic|stack)\\\\s+:(green|red|error)',part)\n assert len(states)==3 and len(set(states))==1,part\n return states[0]\nprovenance=rows(full,'PROVENANCE ')\npairs={row_id(r):r for r in rows(full,'EXCEPTION-PAIR ')}\nreplacement=rows(rerun,'EXCEPTION-PAIR ')\nassert len(provenance)==47 and len(pairs)==46 and len(replacement)==7\nfor r in replacement:\n assert row_id(r).startswith('[:typescript :python ')\n pairs[row_id(r)]=r\nall_rows=provenance+list(pairs.values())\nassert len(set(map(row_id,all_rows)))==93\nassert all('(get ' not in r and '(= ' not in r and '#object' not in r for r in all_rows)\ncounts=collections.Counter(status(r) for r in all_rows)\nassert counts=={'green':27,'red':53,'error':13},counts\nassert re.search(r'Ran 10 tests containing 279 assertions.\\\\n138 failures, 60 errors.',full)\nassert re.search(r'Ran 1 tests containing 21 assertions.\\\\n21 failures, 0 errors.',rerun)\nfronts=['clojure','php','python','typescript']\nscenarios=['binding','catch-all','finally-replacement','retained-lifetime','round-trip','success-raise-success','typed-catch','unchanged-rethrow']\nexpected_pairs={f'[:{d} :{c} :{s}]' for d in fronts for c in fronts if d\"'!=c and '\"'python' in [d,c] for s in scenarios if not(s=='binding' and d=='typescript') and not(s=='finally-replacement' and c=='clojure')}\nassert set(pairs)==expected_pairs\npending=[f'[:{d} :{c}]' for d in fronts for c in fronts if d\"'!=c and '\"'python' not in [d,c]]\nstatuses='\\\\n'.join(f'  {row_id(r)} :{status(r)}' for r in all_rows)\nledger='''{:authority \\\"collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md\\\"\n :ruling-commit \\\"4879edef\\\"\n :base \\\"7ab37566\\\"\n :branch \\\"exception-r0\\\"\n :session-id \\\"01a1b40e-37dc-7be1-8dd7-d0beac15afc5\\\"\n :host :jvm\n :backends #{:semantic :stack :register}\n :verification\n {:full-run {:tests 10 :assertions 279 :failures 138 :errors 60\n             :superseded-direction [:typescript :python]}\n  :corrected-direction {:tests 1 :assertions 21 :failures 21 :errors 0\n                        :direction [:typescript :python]}\n  :accepted-runtime {:test-vars 10 :case-rows 93 :assertions 279\n                     :passes 81 :failures 159 :errors 39}\n  :green-regressions {:test-vars 10 :assertions 135 :failures 0 :errors 0}}\n :pending-scenario-rows 44\n :pending-directions ['''+' '.join(pending)+''']\n :runtime-repair-gates\n {:typescript #{:yang.call.exception-contract/r1 :yang.call.exception-contract/r3}\n  :php #{:yang.call.exception-contract/r1 :yang.call.exception-contract/r2 :yang.call.exception-contract/r3}\n  :python #{:yang.call.exception-contract/r2 :yang.call.exception-contract/r3}\n  :clojure #{:yang.call.exception-contract/r3 :yang.call.exception-contract/r4}}\n :status-by-id {\n'''+statuses+'''}\n :provenance [\n'''+ '\\\\n'.join(provenance)+''']\n :python-pairs [\n'''+ '\\\\n'.join(pairs[k] for k in sorted(pairs))+''']}\n'''\n(root/'exception_r0_results.edn').write_text(ledger)\n# Check balanced EDN delimiters outside strings; every row is Clojure pr-str.\nstack=[]; quoted=False; escaped=False\nfor c in ledger:\n if quoted:\n  if escaped: escaped=False\n  elif c=='\\\\\\\\': escaped=True\n  elif c=='\\\"': quoted=False\n  continue\n if c=='\\\"': quoted=True\n elif c in '([{': stack.append(c)\n elif c in ')]}':\n  assert stack.pop()=='({['[')}]'.index(c)]\nassert not stack and not quoted\nreport=root/'EXCEPTION_R0.md'\ns=report.read_text()\ns+='''\n\n### Exact runtime verification counts\n\nThe complete run (\"'`-n yang.call.exception-contract-test -n\nyang.python.antlr.exception-call-test`) produced **10 tests / 279 assertions,\n138 failures / 60 errors**. Its seven JavaScript-to-Python rows were setup\nerrors: the kit projected JavaScript'\"'s absent \"'`needs_argument` export. The\nlanded `exception-legs/donor-exports` follows the actual donor capability.\nThose seven obsolete rows are replaced by the corrected targeted run:\n\n```\nclj -M:test -n yang.python.antlr.exception-call-test '\"\\\\\\\\\n  -v yang.python.antlr.exception-call-test/typescript-to-python-test\n\"'```\n\nThat run produced **1 test / 21 assertions, 21 failures / 0 errors**. No\nother executed direction'\"'s source or projections changed. Final kit/source\nverification was rerun after this correction and remained **6 / 131, green**.\n\nThe current, deduplicated runtime ledger therefore has **93 rows × 3 VMs =\n279 assertions: 81 pass, 159 fail, 39 operational errors**. Its 47 provenance\nrows are 11 green / 29 red / 7 error; its 46 Python-containing source-pair\nrows are 16 green / 24 red / 6 error. All three VMs agree on every row's\nstatus. With the 135 green regression/helper assertions, the final unique\ncoverage is **20 test vars / 414 assertions: 216 pass, 159 fail, 39 error**.\nThis aggregate combines the full run with the corrected direction; it is\nnot a claim that a single post-correction full-suite command was run.\n\n\"'`exception_r0_results.edn` records the expected values, actual observations,\ngates, frontend sets, backend statuses, verification counts, and the\nID-to-status map. The rejected setup-error rows are absent from its current\ninventory. Feed `:status-by-id` to `exception-contract/open-gates`; unreported\nand pending obligations remain open.\n\n### Fixture inventory\n\nEach state below holds on semantic, stack, and register. **Error** means a\nfailing test with the original host refusal, not a guest thrown condition.\nR5 throw/forgery reds in JS/PHP are blocked by R1'\"'s missing bridge.\n\n| Fixture ID | Gates | Frontend | Current status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n'''\nfor r in sorted(provenance,key=row_id):\n rid=row_id(r)\n gates='/'.join(g.upper() for g in re.findall(r':yang.call.exception-contract/(r[1-5])',r[:r.index(':frontends')]))\n front=rid[1:].split('/')[0]\n s+=f'| \"'`{rid}` | {gates} | {front} | {status(r)} |'\"\\\\n'\ns+='''\n### Python source-pair report\n\nG = green; R = condition/transfer mismatch; E = original host operational\nerror; — = not applicable to the admitted source capability. Every cell\nrepresents three VM assertions. JS's typed-catch row exercises its admitted\nuntyped catch; Clojure uses its single \"'`Exception` catch and no `finally`.\n\n| Scenario | Python→JS | JS→Python | Python→PHP | PHP→Python | Python→Clojure | Clojure→Python |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n'\"'''\ndirections=[('python','typescript'),('typescript','python'),('python','php'),('php','python'),('python','clojure'),('clojure','python')]\nletters={'green':'G','red':'R','error':'E'}\nfor scenario in scenarios:\n cells=[]\n for d,c in directions:\n  row=pairs.get(f'[:{d} :{c} :{scenario}]')\n  cells.append(letters[status(row)] if row else '—')\n s+=f'| \"'`{scenario}` | '\"'+' | '.join(cells)+' |\\\\n'\ns+='''\nClojure→Python's typed reception, stored-wrapper lifetime, and unchanged\nrethrow are R2 reds: the otherwise-foreign cell is raised raw at Python\n\"'`prelude.cljc:1045`; the catch-entry counter prevents an uncaught raw escape\nfrom falsely passing rethrow. Python'\"'s isolated protocol fixtures separately\npin the R3 TypeError loss at \"'`:1046` and always-fresh egress at `:912`.\n\nPython→JS'\"'s four reds and all JS→Python/ PHP→Python reds are missing-bridge\nR1 failures (including cleanup bypass on A→B→A). Python→PHP's six E cases\nare envelope class-checking failures at PHP \"'`prelude.cljc:143` / `:4147`;\nfinally replacement and round trip instead expose the missing bridge.\nPython→Clojure'\"'s seven greens close only these scenarios: Clojure R3 and R4\nremain open. The remaining six directed pairs' 44 scenarios are authored,\nparse/lower successfully, and stay pending their rounds.\n\n### Acceptance-ledger seed\n\n| Frontend | Runtime repairs still open | Full acceptance still open |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| JavaScript (\"'`:typescript`) | R1, R3 | R1, R2, R3, R5 |\n| PHP | R1, R2, R3 | R1, R2, R3, R5 |\n| Python | R2, R3, including egress | R1, R2, R3, R5 |\n| Clojure | R3, then R4 | R1, R2, R3, R4, R5 |\n\nFull acceptance includes the pending directions, capabilities, complete\ncontext snapshots, formatting/forgery probes, and host/publication/custody\nobligations above. No frontend is declared conformant by this Round 0 seed.\n'\"'''\nreport.write_text(s)\nprint('Accepted runtime cases:',dict(counts))\nprint('Runtime assertions:',{k:v*3 for k,v in counts.items()})\nprint('Wrote',root/'exception_r0_results.edn','and',report)\nPY\n\ngit diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
